 139 \u8211? Ticking Clock \par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
 Particularly important is006 \u8211? Foreshadowing. To paraphrase Chekhov, if there is a rifle hanging on the wall in the first act, it absolutely must go off in the second act. If the rifle is not going to be fired, it shouldn\u8217?t be hanging there. \par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
 Planting and removing elements ones is mostly done during re-writings, because you will only know what\u8217?s important and what\u8217?s not after you\u8217?ve finished the first draft. \par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
