 {\b
Description:} \par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
 Snakes have represented evil since time immemorial\u8212?an archetypical association with the danger they embody. Myth echoes that primal fear by surrounding the figure of the Villain with this symbolism. \par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
 If it fits the genre of your story (like fantasy, for example), put at least one snake, serpent, reptile, or dragon in there. If such creatures would look out of place in your story, for example in a romantic comedy, or in a war story happening inside a submarine, then include them anyway, but make it subtle. \par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
 Instead of reptiles, some stories include skulls, spiders, ghosts, monsters, vampires, or a legendary creature, like the Golem or Bigfoot. \par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
