 Farewell \par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
W e arrive at our own{\i
d\u233?nouemen}{\i
t}, too. \par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
 I\u8217?m writing these words with a smile and a bit of sadness, because when we finish a book, we too resist going back to the Ordinary World\u8212?just like the heroes we followed along these pages. Yes, ending a book (either writing or reading it) is a bittersweet moment, indeed. Doesn\u8217?t that happen to you, too? \par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
 But hey, this is our guided return: Let\u8217?s go back to reading great novels and watching great movies. Let\u8217?s enjoy those beautiful stories, this time with a deeper understanding of what makes them tick. \par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
 And remember: I tried my best, but \u8220?Nobody can advise you and help you\u8212?nobody,\u8221? Rilke said a century ago in his{\i
Letters to a Young Poe}{\i
t}. \u8220?There is only one way. Go into yourself.\u8221? \par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
 So this is my Call to Adventure to you, young Padawan: With a laptop for your lightsaber and black coffee as your Elixir, go find inspiration and write, if that what\u8217?s you are meant to do. Let your fantasy take off, rising on its own Magic Flight. \par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
 Thanks for reading my book. Now it is time to face our dragons and go and write some more. \par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
 I believe in you. \par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
